WEBVTT

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:22.730
It sounds like fun, Brother.

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:27.730
Yes. It looks as though I will be relying
heavily on your advice for this.

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:30.350
I will be counting on you, William.

00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:36.020
Of course. This all started
at your request, after all.

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:38.850
Louis, I'll be expecting
much of you, as well.

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:40.850
Yes, Brother.

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:43.690
We share the same goal,

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:49.560
as well as our past,
our present, and our future.

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:57.810
For we three brothers
are "James Moriarty."

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:35.960
A Scandal in the British Empire Act 2

00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:39.520
Please refrain from speaking anyone's
true names whilst inside today,

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:44.150
bearing in mind that this is meant
to be a masquerade ball.

00:02:44.150 --> 00:02:47.060
Also, as part of our regular
entertainment this evening,

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:49.940
we will be playing a riddle-solving game.

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:56.150
Tonight's theme... is the Lord of Crime,
who is the talk of the town.

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:59.150
The mysterious figure who
is rumoured to have his hand

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:03.190
in half of the crime that is
now taking place in London.

00:03:03.190 --> 00:03:08.730
The rules are simple: One of our guests
is chosen to play the Lord of Crime,

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:12.770
and that person will commit "murder."

00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:17.400
Any guest who is "murdered" will
reveal their face before all of us,

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:20.770
and then kindly relocate
to the upper floor.

00:03:20.770 --> 00:03:24.310
Following that, they will no longer
be able to attend the ball,

00:03:24.310 --> 00:03:27.230
and must donate the most
costly item they are wearing

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:33.020
toward the college now under
construction as a penalty.

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:37.350
Further, once the rest of you determine
the Lord of Crime's identity,

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:41.400
they will "die," and the game
will come to an end.

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:44.730
We will have to do our best to find them.

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:48.270
Yes. This should be quite fun.

00:03:56.520 --> 00:04:01.270
I understand that currently,
the Yard has no clues as to his identity.

00:04:01.270 --> 00:04:03.560
Some of the townsfolk
say that he is a hero,

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:06.980
set on exposing the dark deeds
of the upper class.

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:10.980
Right now, he is apparently as well-liked
as the Great Detective Holmes.

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:14.730
As sort of a symbol representing
light and darkness.

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:19.940
The rumours sure are buzzing. That's the
ruler of London's underworld for you.

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:23.850
Hmph, rubbish! "Lord of Crime," my eye.

00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:27.520
A criminal, getting the
Robin Hood treatment?

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:30.100
It is unsurprising.

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:34.520
The noblemen who were killed
were all embroiled in scandals.

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:37.730
It is only natural for the townsfolk
to regard the Lord of Crime...

00:04:37.730 --> 00:04:39.480
...as a chivalrous thief.

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:45.310
Ha! It sounds like you're saying
that it was only right that they died.

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:47.440
Nothing of the sort.

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:52.190
Who is this young lad?
Such a disagreeable twit.

00:04:52.190 --> 00:04:57.560
Hmph, he doesn't even know I was
picked to be the Lord of Crime.

00:04:57.560 --> 00:05:01.270
That clinches it. My very first victim...

00:05:01.270 --> 00:05:03.020
...will be <i>him</i> .

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:28.600
Is something the matter?

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:30.440
No...

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:33.350
Ladies and gentlemen!
Your attention, please!

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:35.690
Regarding tonight's riddle-solving game,

00:05:35.690 --> 00:05:40.230
our Lord of Crime's first heinous act
has already been completed.

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:45.310
The mark of our first victim is wine.

00:05:45.310 --> 00:05:48.730
Anyone who has had wine splashed
on them has been murdered.

00:05:48.730 --> 00:05:51.980
Everyone please check those
who are around you.

00:05:51.980 --> 00:05:53.400
Wine, is it?

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:56.310
I haven't any on me.

00:05:56.310 --> 00:05:59.940
Would you mind looking at my back?

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:02.520
Oh! Oh, dear!

00:06:03.940 --> 00:06:07.770
It would appear that
I am the first victim.

00:06:07.770 --> 00:06:10.480
Huh? Not Lord Moriarty!

00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:13.480
Who would splash wine on Lord Moriarty?

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:20.190
I am Albert James Moriarty. They got me!

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:23.900
No! Lord Moriarty!

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:28.730
Ah, yes, the donation. Will this ring do?

00:06:28.730 --> 00:06:33.770
Thank you very much. It will, indeed.

00:06:33.770 --> 00:06:37.770
I didn't expect that
youngster to be an earl.

00:06:37.770 --> 00:06:41.850
Can we please have a round
of applause for Lord Moriarty?

00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:45.150
Me, too!

00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:51.230
It seems that I, too, have fallen
victim to the Lord of Crime!

00:06:51.230 --> 00:06:55.560
Hmm? I don't remember
splashing any on him.

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:08.100
So you adopted a second persona
to come here tonight, did you...

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:11.100
...Irene Adler?

00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:15.690
You could have taken me into
your custody at Baker Street.

00:07:15.690 --> 00:07:20.850
The fact that you didn't shows that you
do not wish to deal roughly with me.

00:07:20.850 --> 00:07:25.100
Additionally, thanks to you arranging
this anonymous affair,

00:07:25.100 --> 00:07:29.400
I decided that I could trust you
as someone I could negotiate with.

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:31.480
A judicious decision.

00:07:31.480 --> 00:07:35.270
I have been charged by the
government with this matter.

00:07:35.270 --> 00:07:40.230
You may freely take my word to be
the word of the British government.

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:45.850
Are you willing to return the papers
you stole from the palace?

00:07:45.850 --> 00:07:49.730
Of course. However,
I have some conditions.

00:07:49.730 --> 00:07:54.060
Firstly, you must guarantee my safety.

00:07:54.060 --> 00:07:58.350
Secondly, you must overlook
the crime of my theft.

00:07:58.350 --> 00:08:02.940
If you will observe these two conditions,
I will return them at once.

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:11.850
My answer, on behalf of the government...

00:08:11.850 --> 00:08:13.520
...is no.

00:08:15.020 --> 00:08:19.230
I was afforded no room to bargain
in this matter from the very start.

00:08:19.230 --> 00:08:25.770
The orders I was issued were to take back
the papers, and to liquidate you.

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:28.690
Then why did you call me here?!

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:31.440
Whilst I am an agent of the government,

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:34.690
it was not in that capacity
that I summoned you.

00:08:36.230 --> 00:08:39.560
I had my reservations from the outset.

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:45.060
Why did the thief who stole the documents
choose not to do anything?

00:08:45.060 --> 00:08:49.900
She gave no demands, nor did she
claim responsibility for the theft.

00:08:49.900 --> 00:08:52.560
Why would that be?

00:08:52.560 --> 00:08:54.230
Because the thief likely realised

00:08:54.230 --> 00:08:58.150
that the content of the papers
was beyond what she could handle,

00:08:58.150 --> 00:09:02.020
and was seeking a safer
means of returning them.

00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:05.020
But now that it is no longer possible
to cast aside the prospect

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:07.650
that you have learnt some state secret,

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:12.480
overlooking your crime
and guaranteeing your safety

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:14.060
would be asking the impossible.

00:09:14.060 --> 00:09:18.480
Then you are only here to inform me
directly that I have no hope of--

00:09:18.480 --> 00:09:20.730
No, I did not.

00:09:21.940 --> 00:09:26.150
I am here to say that
I am able to save you.

00:09:26.150 --> 00:09:30.020
Save... <i>me</i> ...?

00:09:30.020 --> 00:09:33.650
However, it all depends
on just how critical

00:09:33.650 --> 00:09:38.020
the content of those
papers is to the nation.

00:09:38.020 --> 00:09:42.520
But if you find that out, you will be
placed in the same position that I'm in.

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:48.690
No matter. Tell me what
those papers contain first.

00:09:50.310 --> 00:09:54.230
I promise you, you will regret
what you're about to hear.

00:10:08.600 --> 00:10:11.150
So it is not some scandal
about the royal family,

00:10:11.150 --> 00:10:14.940
but a scandal concerning the
entire British Empire, is it?

00:10:16.440 --> 00:10:20.520
Are you truly able to save me?

00:10:20.520 --> 00:10:21.980
Of course.

00:10:21.980 --> 00:10:26.690
Allow me to show you a sampling
of the power that can save you.

00:10:27.940 --> 00:10:30.270
Look down there...

00:10:30.270 --> 00:10:33.400
...at that man in the white mask.

00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:37.190
That is Baron Ronald Rollinson--

00:10:37.190 --> 00:10:41.190
the "Lord of Crime" for
tonight's riddle-solving game.

00:10:41.190 --> 00:10:42.690
How do you know that?

00:10:42.690 --> 00:10:48.440
Why, because I am one of the hosts,
but that is not what I was getting at.

00:10:48.440 --> 00:10:53.190
The man operates opera houses in
both America and France, as well,

00:10:53.190 --> 00:10:56.270
and has a cruel and
self-serving personality.

00:10:56.270 --> 00:10:57.810
About five years ago,

00:10:57.810 --> 00:11:01.270
he set fire to one of his theatres
for the insurance money,

00:11:01.270 --> 00:11:07.150
making it look like it was an accident,
killing many who were inside.

00:11:07.150 --> 00:11:12.270
I know the fire you mean.
Some of my friends were victims.

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:15.520
Are you saying that man did it?

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:17.150
It's time.

00:11:17.150 --> 00:11:19.440
Watch carefully now.

00:11:21.150 --> 00:11:25.230
Ladies and gentlemen, our Lord
of Crime has been caught at last!

00:11:25.230 --> 00:11:31.020
Our Lord of Crime has been
Baron Ronald Rollinson!

00:11:31.020 --> 00:11:35.900
The Lord of Crime expires,
and peace returns once again to London!

00:11:35.900 --> 00:11:38.770
You are all the winners!

00:11:38.770 --> 00:11:41.270
I had no idea at all it was you.

00:11:44.060 --> 00:11:47.520
Is something the matter?
You look a bit pale.

00:11:49.940 --> 00:11:53.440
There you go again. You can stop acting.

00:11:53.440 --> 00:11:58.060
C-Can't breathe...

00:12:02.980 --> 00:12:05.440
--How dreadful. What a ghastly expression.
--H-He's not breathing.

00:12:05.440 --> 00:12:06.350
Huh?

00:12:06.350 --> 00:12:09.560
Baron? Baron! Answer me!

00:12:09.560 --> 00:12:12.900
Hey, someone call a doctor!

00:12:12.900 --> 00:12:16.600
What did you think of that performance?

00:12:16.600 --> 00:12:20.650
Baron Rollinson played his part
as the main character exquisitely.

00:12:20.650 --> 00:12:24.600
As did the other noblemen who were killed.

00:12:24.600 --> 00:12:30.350
And now, I have pronounced the
same punishment on him, as well.

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:36.100
It can't be... Is he...?

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:40.980
Yes. I set this entire thing up.

00:12:40.980 --> 00:12:46.060
Me, the Lord of Crime, James Moriarty.

00:12:47.350 --> 00:12:50.520
You're... the Lord of Crime?

00:12:50.520 --> 00:12:52.230
Have a look.

00:12:56.560 --> 00:12:59.060
Even when a man dies,
the aristocracy of this nation

00:12:59.060 --> 00:13:02.020
continue their party
without a second thought.

00:13:02.020 --> 00:13:06.730
They all are interested only
in themselves. Which means...

00:13:06.730 --> 00:13:09.770
...no matter how many
aristocrats get killed like this,

00:13:09.770 --> 00:13:12.440
there is no changing them.

00:13:12.440 --> 00:13:16.810
"Aristocracy" does not refer
to the people themselves,

00:13:16.810 --> 00:13:19.730
but to the very concept they embody.

00:13:21.270 --> 00:13:27.020
A person cannot kill
an intangible concept.

00:13:27.020 --> 00:13:32.310
Your objective is the
same as mine, is it not?

00:13:32.310 --> 00:13:37.270
My objective is to fundamentally
change this nation.

00:13:37.270 --> 00:13:40.480
I seek to move it from a society
based on the outdated right of blood

00:13:40.480 --> 00:13:43.940
to a free society, based on one's merits.

00:13:43.940 --> 00:13:48.690
The method that I use to
bring reform to this world...

00:13:48.690 --> 00:13:51.770
...is crime.

00:13:51.770 --> 00:13:57.400
Just as <i>you</i> resort to theft, extortion,
and other crimes as your methods.

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:03.650
Changing the world through crime...

00:14:03.650 --> 00:14:05.810
He might just do it, too...

00:14:07.940 --> 00:14:11.190
Forgive me for speaking at such length.

00:14:11.190 --> 00:14:13.520
I will be waiting for you

00:14:13.520 --> 00:14:18.600
in the church along New North Road
in Hoxton at five o'clock, before dawn.

00:14:18.600 --> 00:14:23.400
You have neither time
nor other options remaining.

00:14:23.400 --> 00:14:26.440
I do hope you will choose wisely.

00:14:33.940 --> 00:14:38.060
Lord Albert James Moriarty...

00:14:38.060 --> 00:14:40.480
The Lord of Crime is a nobleman?

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:44.650
One who has worked his way into
the heart of the government, at that.

00:14:44.650 --> 00:14:49.100
And now, he is trying to change the world.

00:14:59.100 --> 00:15:03.270
First, I need to get the papers
without Sherlock and the others seeing.

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:25.980
Sherlock!

00:15:28.310 --> 00:15:31.730
I-Irene... run...!

00:15:31.730 --> 00:15:36.310
He said we were dead
unless we turned you over...

00:15:36.310 --> 00:15:39.520
I told him I didn't know you...
and turned him away...

00:15:39.520 --> 00:15:42.560
He had the moves of
someone who was trained...

00:15:42.560 --> 00:15:45.810
It was all we could do to turn him back...

00:15:45.810 --> 00:15:49.270
I can't believe he planted a bomb, too...

00:15:49.270 --> 00:15:54.810
I thought he was just bluffing...
but he meant business...

00:15:54.810 --> 00:15:58.230
You have to...
You at least have to get away...

00:15:58.230 --> 00:15:59.480
I couldn't!

00:15:59.480 --> 00:16:01.020
Hurry!

00:16:05.020 --> 00:16:07.650
It's my fault that they
got dragged into this.

00:16:07.650 --> 00:16:10.810
I can't let anything else happen to them!

00:16:22.690 --> 00:16:26.940
I see, so that's where you were hiding it.

00:16:26.940 --> 00:16:29.560
Sherlock... Why?

00:16:29.560 --> 00:16:35.310
I finally tripped you up, Irene.
This time, I really have won.

00:16:35.310 --> 00:16:39.980
Honestly, blowing up the second floor
just to trick Miss Adler...

00:16:39.980 --> 00:16:42.730
I thought you were mad
when you proposed it,

00:16:42.730 --> 00:16:44.770
but I'm glad to see it worked.

00:16:44.770 --> 00:16:47.100
Miss Hudson gave us
a stellar performance, as well.

00:16:47.100 --> 00:16:50.940
After you blew up my home,
I wasn't about to mess that up!

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:56.100
Y-You went this far to... Why?

00:16:56.100 --> 00:17:00.650
Why, to protect you,
of course, Miss Adler.

00:17:00.650 --> 00:17:02.940
To protect me?

00:17:02.940 --> 00:17:05.900
I knew that there was
something else motivating you

00:17:05.900 --> 00:17:08.440
besides the photo of the King of Bohemia.

00:17:08.440 --> 00:17:11.560
Which meant that the king's
request meant nothing.

00:17:11.560 --> 00:17:14.810
It stood to reason that he was a
perpetrator that you had put up to this.

00:17:14.810 --> 00:17:19.150
Which would mean that your real
objective was to get close to me,

00:17:19.150 --> 00:17:22.060
something unfathomable at first blush.

00:17:22.060 --> 00:17:25.690
Other than my powers of deduction, the
thing about myself that could be useful,

00:17:25.690 --> 00:17:29.940
much as I hate to say it myself,
is my level of popularity.

00:17:29.940 --> 00:17:32.650
So there is someone who cannot
try anything rough against you,

00:17:32.650 --> 00:17:35.730
so long as you are with one of
the famous people of London.

00:17:35.730 --> 00:17:39.060
In other words, whoever is after you,

00:17:39.060 --> 00:17:43.310
they aren't the minions of the mafia or
the nobility, who would stop at nothing.

00:17:43.310 --> 00:17:44.480
No.

00:17:44.480 --> 00:17:47.650
So why is it that the British
government is out to get you?

00:17:47.650 --> 00:17:51.190
In order to bring that reason to light,
we pretended to come under attack,

00:17:51.190 --> 00:17:54.440
and got you to fall for it.

00:17:54.440 --> 00:17:57.020
What is this, exactly?

00:17:57.020 --> 00:18:01.350
Don't look! If you look at those,
there's no going back!

00:18:01.350 --> 00:18:04.270
They'll end up coming after you, too!

00:18:04.270 --> 00:18:08.350
Ha! I blew up my room to
get my hands on this secret.

00:18:08.350 --> 00:18:11.150
Do you think I'm concerned about
who might come after me?

00:18:12.440 --> 00:18:14.810
Tactical plans?

00:18:14.810 --> 00:18:15.810
Yes.

00:18:15.810 --> 00:18:18.600
A hundred years ago,
the glorious British Empire

00:18:18.600 --> 00:18:22.520
secretly manipulated the French
Revolution from the shadows.

00:18:22.520 --> 00:18:24.100
Those are the plans for it.

00:18:24.100 --> 00:18:27.190
Huh? Why was there any need for that?

00:18:27.190 --> 00:18:29.690
It's quite simple, Louis.

00:18:29.690 --> 00:18:33.270
It was a social experiment.
One to find out what would happen

00:18:33.270 --> 00:18:36.230
if an oppressive, absolute
monarchy were to shift

00:18:36.230 --> 00:18:40.350
to become a republic,
oriented around the citizenry.

00:18:40.350 --> 00:18:46.350
Perhaps the British government's plan
was meant to trigger a revolution.

00:18:46.350 --> 00:18:51.690
Or, it may have only been to throw the
ensuing French government into turmoil.

00:18:52.770 --> 00:18:58.810
Whatever the case, we need to get our
hands on those papers immediately.

00:18:58.810 --> 00:19:02.980
There is no turning back for us now.

00:19:08.690 --> 00:19:12.600
Why do you have a document
as outrageous as this?!

00:19:12.600 --> 00:19:15.480
I stole it from the palace.

00:19:15.480 --> 00:19:19.190
It's not as though I stole it
because I knew what was inside.

00:19:19.190 --> 00:19:22.600
I just needed something with which
to blackmail the prince, that's all.

00:19:22.600 --> 00:19:28.650
B-Blackmail the prince?
For what reason, exactly?

00:19:28.650 --> 00:19:31.520
I wanted to reform the world.

00:19:31.520 --> 00:19:34.810
It's what I have always done.

00:19:34.810 --> 00:19:36.850
It started when one of the
actresses I performed with

00:19:36.850 --> 00:19:41.190
was driven to take her own life simply
because she was from a common family.

00:19:41.190 --> 00:19:45.440
No matter how much work she put in,
she was never given her proper due.

00:19:45.440 --> 00:19:50.810
So I had to urge those doing the
criticising--the nobility--to come around.

00:19:50.810 --> 00:19:56.350
I used my feminine allure to exploit
the upper class's weaknesses,

00:19:56.350 --> 00:19:58.190
and ingratiated myself to them.

00:19:58.190 --> 00:20:01.100
Doing so, I was able to support those
who could not get ahead,

00:20:01.100 --> 00:20:03.770
whether due to financial or class reasons,

00:20:03.770 --> 00:20:08.560
working to ensure that their talents
and efforts would bear fruit.

00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:12.100
You did something as grand
as that all by yourself?

00:20:12.100 --> 00:20:15.020
No, John, she's telling the truth.

00:20:15.020 --> 00:20:20.520
Having heard this,
my profile of her finally fits.

00:20:20.520 --> 00:20:23.400
This one time, I thought that
if I could influence the prince,

00:20:23.400 --> 00:20:25.400
I could change the country,

00:20:25.400 --> 00:20:29.150
but ended up stealing something
too big for me to handle.

00:20:29.150 --> 00:20:30.900
What a fool I was.

00:20:30.900 --> 00:20:34.230
Then I wound up dragging
all of you into this, as well.

00:20:36.810 --> 00:20:39.150
I am sorry.

00:20:39.150 --> 00:20:40.770
Miss Adler...

00:20:40.770 --> 00:20:44.650
So, where have you been all evening?

00:20:48.150 --> 00:20:51.020
The government has guaranteed
that they would spare my life

00:20:51.020 --> 00:20:55.310
on condition that I turn over
the papers you're holding,

00:20:55.310 --> 00:20:58.520
as well as provide all the information
that I have obtained.

00:20:58.520 --> 00:21:02.480
Please, without that, my life is over!

00:21:02.480 --> 00:21:05.190
Give it back, Sherlock.

00:21:22.650 --> 00:21:26.350
Are you sure about this,
Sherlock--returning that to her?

00:21:28.400 --> 00:21:32.310
Is this for real? No more
monkeying around, damn it!

00:21:32.310 --> 00:21:34.600
There isn't any other
choice at this point.

00:21:34.600 --> 00:21:38.980
However, what she said is clearly untrue!

00:21:38.980 --> 00:21:40.480
What was untrue about it?

00:21:40.480 --> 00:21:44.520
What she said about reasoning
with the government was untrue.

00:21:44.520 --> 00:21:50.850
Remember me saying so before?
The government-- <i>he</i> is not that simple.

00:21:50.850 --> 00:21:54.850
Which means that she has found
someone else to deal with.

00:21:54.850 --> 00:21:57.850
Someone else? Who, then?

00:21:57.850 --> 00:22:02.520
Think about it, John. Someone who
wants that godforsaken document,

00:22:02.520 --> 00:22:07.190
and has enough influence to protect Irene
from the government's clutches.

00:22:07.190 --> 00:22:11.060
Yes, Irene is dealing with...

00:22:12.350 --> 00:22:14.270
...the Lord of Crime!

00:23:46.020 --> 00:23:52.030
A Scandal in the British Empire Act 3

00:23:46.730 --> 00:23:52.230
Next time on <i>Moriarty the Patriot</i> :
"A Scandal in the British Empire Act 3."
